From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FluxCast maintainers <noreply@fluxcast.local>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 20:35:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] evdi: reject imported GEM mmap before pinning pages

evdi_gem_mmap() cannot expose imported DMA-BUF objects through the dumb
GEM mmap-offset interface. Check import_attach before evdi_pin_pages():
the previous order incremented pages_pin_count and returned -EINVAL
without releasing that pin for every rejected imported object.

Keep the rejection and its diagnostic unchanged; DMA-BUF CPU access must
use the dedicated DMA-BUF mapping path with the exporter's synchronization
contract, not this dumb-buffer mmap ioctl.
---
 module/evdi_gem.c | 14 +++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/module/evdi_gem.c b/module/evdi_gem.c
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/module/evdi_gem.c
+++ b/module/evdi_gem.c
@@ -482,15 +482,15 @@ int evdi_gem_mmap(struct drm_file *file,
 	if (obj == NULL)
 		return -ENOENT;
 	gobj = to_evdi_bo(obj);
 
-	ret = evdi_pin_pages(gobj);
-	if (ret)
-		goto out;
-
 	/* Don't allow imported objects to be mapped */
 	if (obj->import_attach) {
-		EVDI_WARN("Don't allow imported objects to be mapped: owner: %s\n",  obj->import_attach->dmabuf->owner->name);
+		const char *owner = "unknown";
+
+		if (obj->import_attach->dmabuf->owner)
+			owner = obj->import_attach->dmabuf->owner->name;
+		EVDI_WARN("Rejecting imported GEM mmap: owner=%s caller=%s[%d]\n",
+			  owner, current->comm, task_pid_nr(current));
 		ret = -EINVAL;
 		goto out;
 	}
 
+	ret = evdi_pin_pages(gobj);
+	if (ret)
+		goto out;
+
 	ret = drm_gem_create_mmap_offset(obj);
 	if (ret)
 		goto out;
